        "embed_id": "bed8cbe3-2ce3-47f0-ac01-1b864a17e574",
        "type": "notebook",
        "content": "type: notebook\napp_id: code\nskill_id: notebook\nlanguage: python\nfilename: open_meteo_weather_analysis.ipynb\ncell_count: 7\nembed_ref: open_meteo_weather_analysis.ipynb-bed8cb\nstatus: finished\nsource_version: null\nnotebook:\n  cells[7]:\n    - cell_type: markdown\n      metadata:\n      source[3]: \"# Berlin 7-Day Weather Analysis & Weekend Bike Ride Planner\\n\",\"\\n\",\"This notebook fetches the next 7 days of hourly weather forecasts for Berlin from the free [Open-Meteo API](https://open-meteo.com/) (no API key required). We will process the JSON response using `requests` and `pandas`, calculate daily aggregates (min/max temperatures and total precipitation), visualize the forecast, and evaluate whether the upcoming conditions are suitable for a weekend bike ride.\"\n    - cell_type: code\n      execution_count: null\n      metadata:\n      outputs[0]:\n      source[27]: \"import requests\\n\",\"import pandas as pd\\n\",\"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n\",\"\\n\",\"# 1. Fetch hourly forecast for Berlin (Latitude: 52.52, Longitude: 13.405)\\n\",\"url = \\\"https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast\\\"\\n\",\"params = {\\n\",\"    \\\"latitude\\\": 52.52,\\n\",\"    \\\"longitude\\\": 13.405,\\n\",\"    \\\"hourly\\\": \\\"temperature_2m,precipitation,wind_speed_10m,cloud_cover\\\",\\n\",\"    \\\"timezone\\\": \\\"Europe/Berlin\\\"\\n\",\"}\\n\",\"\\n\",\"response = requests.get(url, params=params)\\n\",\"data = response.json()\\n\",\"\\n\",\"# 2. Load hourly data into a pandas DataFrame\\n\",\"hourly_data = data[\\\"hourly\\\"]\\n\",\"df_hourly = pd.DataFrame({\\n\",\"    \\\"time\\\": pd.to_datetime(hourly_data[\\\"time\\\"]),\\n\",\"    \\\"temperature_2m\\\": hourly_data[\\\"temperature_2m\\\"],\\n\",\"    \\\"precipitation\\\": hourly_data[\\\"precipitation\\\"],\\n\",\"    \\\"wind_speed_10m\\\": hourly_data[\\\"wind_speed_10m\\\"],\\n\",\"    \\\"cloud_cover\\\": hourly_data[\\\"cloud_cover\\\"]\\n\",\"})\\n\",\"\\n\",df_hourly.head()\n    - cell_type: markdown\n      metadata:\n      source[5]: \"## Daily Aggregations\\n\",\"\\n\",\"Next, we resample or group our hourly data by calendar day to compute:\\n\",\"- **Minimum and Maximum Temperature** (°C)\\n\",\"- **Total Daily Precipitation** (mm)\"\n    - cell_type: code\n      execution_count: null\n      metadata:\n      outputs[0]:\n      source[11]: \"df_hourly[\\\"date\\\"] = df_hourly[\\\"time\\\"].dt.date\\n\",\"\\n\",\"df_daily = df_hourly.groupby(\\\"date\\\").agg(\\n\",\"    temp_min=(\\\"temperature_2m\\\", \\\"min\\\"),\\n\",\"    temp_max=(\\\"temperature_2m\\\", \\\"max\\\"),\\n\",\"    precipitation_sum=(\\\"precipitation\\\", \\\"sum\\\"),\\n\",\"    wind_speed_mean=(\\\"wind_speed_10m\\\", \\\"mean\\\"),\\n\",\"    cloud_cover_mean=(\\\"cloud_cover\\\", \\\"mean\\\")\\n\",\").reset_index()\\n\",\"\\n\",df_daily\n    - cell_type: markdown\n      metadata:\n      source[3]: \"## Weather Visualizations\\n\",\"\\n\",Let's plot the 7-day temperature trend (min/max band or lines) alongside daily precipitation.\n    - cell_type: code\n      execution_count: null\n      metadata:\n      outputs[0]:\n      source[20]: \"fig, ax1 = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 5))\\n\",\"\\n\",\"# Temperature plot\\n\",\"ax1.set_xlabel(\\\"Date\\\")\\n\",\"ax1.set_ylabel(\\\"Temperature (°C)\\\", color=\\\"tab:red\\\")\\n\",\"ax1.plot(df_daily[\\\"date\\\"], df_daily[\\\"temp_max\\\"], color=\\\"tab:red\\\", marker=\\\"o\\\", label=\\\"Max Temp\\\")\\n\",\"ax1.plot(df_daily[\\\"date\\\"], df_daily[\\\"temp_min\\\"], color=\\\"tab:orange\\\", marker=\\\"o\\\", linestyle=\\\"--\\\", label=\\\"Min Temp\\\")\\n\",\"ax1.tick_params(axis=\\\"y\\\", labelcolor=\\\"tab:red\\\")\\n\",\"ax1.legend(loc=\\\"upper left\\\")\\n\",\"plt.xticks(rotation=45)\\n\",\"\\n\",\"# Precipitation plot on secondary axis\\n\",\"ax2 = ax1.twinx()\\n\",\"ax2.set_ylabel(\\\"Precipitation (mm)\\\", color=\\\"tab:blue\\\")\\n\",\"ax2.bar(df_daily[\\\"date\\\"], df_daily[\\\"precipitation_sum\\\"], color=\\\"tab:blue\\\", alpha=0.3, width=0.4, label=\\\"Precipitation\\\")\\n\",\"ax2.tick_params(axis=\\\"y\\\", labelcolor=\\\"tab:blue\\\")\\n\",\"\\n\",\"plt.title(\\\"Berlin 7-Day Temperature and Precipitation Forecast\\\")\\n\",\"fig.tight_layout()\\n\",plt.show()\n    - cell_type: markdown\n      metadata:\n      source[8]: \"## Weekend Bike Ride Assessment\\n\",\"\\n\",\"Based on the generated daily forecast table and plots:\\n\",\"- **Temperature Check:** Look at Saturday and Sunday maximum temperatures. Ideal cycling temperatures typically range between 15°C and 25°C.\\n\",\"- **Rain Check:** Examine the precipitation sum bars for the weekend. Zero or near-zero precipitation indicates dry trails and roads, whereas high rainfall suggests rescheduling or preparing waterproof gear.\\n\",\"- **Wind & Clouds:** Moderate wind speeds (< 20 km/h) make for pleasant riding conditions without heavy resistance.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"*Conclusion:* Check the resulting charts above to pick the optimal day and time window for your weekend ride!\"\n  metadata:\n    language_info:\n      name: python\n  nbformat: 4\n  nbformat_minor: 2",
